    + the settings UnitStore; the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection → MotorHistoryProjectionBuilder.build is a 1:1 port of web `buildChartData`:
    drop rows without ts/created_at, stator = di_stator_temp ?? motor_temp_c_front (SI °C →
    display unit via convertTempFromSI), torque = di_torque, gear = gear ?? shift_state,
    lateral/longitudinal g carried, sorted ascending by time. Latest-value scan (newest-first,
    skip nils), danger threshold (100 °C → display), temp-axis max (danger+20, expanded, ceil).
    Verified by executed XCTest (13) + executed harness (27).
  Composition → WidgetShell chrome (Cog icon + "Motor History" title + freshness chip + refresh +
    optional Open) · WidgetChartSummary stat row (Torque Nm / Stator °unit) · the chart.
    Recharts ComposedChart → Swift Charts: torque LineMark (cyan, left axis), stator LineMark
    (orange, right axis), ReferenceArea danger band > 100 °C (red 10%), wide-mode dashed
    lateral-G (purple) + longitudinal-G (green) overlays. The single Swift Charts Y scale renders
    the web's dual axes faithfully via MotorChartScale (temp ↔ torque plotting space), so the
    right temp axis and the danger band line up exactly with the stator line.
  Shared components → reuses the REAL apps/apple library compiled in GATE [1]/[2]: Color.TS,
